From a61056235a7b883361fb9f722fd0e61a3fd4e61f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:57:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 90/94] consensus: set the validation weight of a rescue check
 to 130,000

At the provisional 100,000 the single-check gate of contrib/m4r-measure
asked for 96,579 to 106,234 on the measuring machine, and the whole-block
gate failed by a hair: a block of rescue checks after Schnorr checks took
1.005 (release) and 1.014 (portable multiplication) times the Schnorr
worst block at the default -par. 130,000 gives both gates a margin and
stays within the bound of 130,333, the budget of the smallest valid
rescue input less 50.

The two_checks vector drops 260 elements instead of 140, so that its
budget still pays for a second rescue check (R3, not R2), the R4 case 260
instead of 200, and the fuzz target p2mr_rescue 260 instead of 150; the
other vectors are unchanged. p2mr-ts's vectors (31e737d) still carry the
provisional 100,000, which the test now names as theirs.
doc/p2mr-rescue.md gives the weight and how it was set.
